# A SIMPLE GUIDE TO THE CDCEAD AND SOCDCEAD APIs

The Composite Data Correspondence Editor (CDCEAD) application programming interface is a general product oriented editing tool based on Common Engine (CE).

If a user starts editing operations, action() is called through CE callback.

A snippet from the CDCEAD source code:

```java
/* Action class to trigger the event flow after edit command is handled */
protected static class triggerUpdateAction extends Action {
    protected void action() {
        SystemConsole.showlog("triggerUpdateAction done");
    }
}
```

The SOCDCEAD (Stand On Composite Data Editors And Devices box) application programming interface combines CDCEAD and the SOCDCE

